<title>GREECE: OLYMPIC AIRWAYS TO PURCHASE TWO NEW A340 AIRBUS JETS.</title>
<headline>OLYMPIC AIRWAYS TO PURCHASE TWO NEW A340 AIRBUS JETS.</headline>
<dateline>ATHENS 1997-07-31</dateline>
<text>
<p>Greece's state carrier Olympic Airways will purchase two new A340 Airbus jets the Athens News Agency (ANA) reported on Thursday.</p>
<p>Transport and communications minister Haris Kastanidis authorised Olympic's board to go ahead with the purchase on the recommendation of the state audit council.</p>
<p>The contract which also contains an option for the purchase of two additional aircraft will be signed in the next few days, ANA said. --George Georgiopoulos, Athens Newsroom +301 3311812-4</p>
</text>
